®MDBO¯CITY COUNCIL APPROVES RIVERFRONT PLAN®MDNM¯
®MDUL¯By the Metro Desk®MDNM¯   (draft, slug: RIVER-PLAN)

The city council voted 7 to 2 on Tuesday night to approve a $14 million plan to rebuild the riverfront, ending three years of debate over parking, flood walls and a proposed bandstand.

Supporters said the plan would bring ®MDBO¯new foot traffic®MDNM¯ to the old warehouse district. Opponents, led by Councilwoman Ruth Avery, argued that the flood wall design had not been reviewed by the state.

"We are building on a promise," Mayor Dan Kessler said after the vote. "The river was the reason this town exists."

®MDUL¯Key points®MDNM¯
  - Construction begins in the spring.
  - The bandstand was dropped from the final plan.
  - Parking moves to a new deck on Water Street.

